impl PowerThrottle {
    /// Returns `true` if validator should decline participation in *future* epochs
    /// MUST NOT affect execution of already-started epochs
    pub fn should_decline_future_epochs(&self) -> bool {
        self.current_temp > self.thermal_limit_celsius ||
        self.current_battery < self.battery_floor_percent
    }
    
    /// Returns `true` if validator must halt immediately (safety override)
    pub fn requires_immediate_halt(&self) -> bool {
        // Critical thermal/battery thresholds that risk hardware damage
        self.current_temp > (self.thermal_limit_celsius + 15) ||
        self.current_battery < (self.battery_floor_percent / 2)
    }
}
```

**Constraint**: Throttling is a *readiness signal* only. It must not modify epoch execution or consensus state.

