## 3. Cryptographic Architecture (REVISED)

### 3.1 Astronomical Cascade Architecture

**Design Principle**: Eliminate single points of cryptographic failure through **hierarchical, depth-parameterized, cross-primitive composition** — not merely parallel execution.

**Cascade Structure**:
```
Level 0 (Input): [validator_id || epoch || epoch_seed || payload]
       │
       ▼
Level 1 (Parallel Primitives): 
   ├─ SHA3-256(input) → h₁
   ├─ BLAKE3(input)   → h₂  
   ├─ KangarooTwelve(input, 32) → h₃
   ├─ SM3(input)      → h₄
   └─ Streebog(input) → h₅
       │
       ▼
Level 2 (Cross-Binding): 
   cascade_layer_2 = H_bind( h₁ || h₂ || h₃ || h₄ || h₅ || domain_separator )
   where H_bind ∈ {SHA3-512, BLAKE3-256} (genesis-pinned)
       │
       ▼
Level 3+ (Recursive Expansion, if cascade_depth > 2):
   For i in 3..cascade_depth:
       cascade_layer_i = H_i( cascade_layer_{i-1} || layer_seed_i || domain_i )
       where H_i cycles through hash_primitives in genesis-pinned order
       │
       ▼
Final Output: cascade_root = cascade_layer_{cascade_depth}
```

**Genesis Configuration**:
```toml
[crypto.cascade]
# Primitive set (parallel at Level 1)
primitives = [
    { name = "SHA3-256", family = "sponge", nist = "FIPS-202" },
    { name = "BLAKE3", family = "ARX", nist = "none" },
    { name = "KangarooTwelve", family = "sponge", nist = "SP-800-185" },
    { name = "SM3", family = "merkle-damgard", nist = "none", jurisdiction = "CN" },
    { name = "Streebog", family = "block-cipher", nist = "none", jurisdiction = "RU" }
]

# Cascade parameters
cascade_depth = 7                    # "Astronomical" depth: 7 layers minimum
