| Layer | What It Sees | Polymorphic Code Role |
|-------|-------------|---------------------|
| **Domain A (Consensus)** | Only `state_root`, `receipt_root`, epoch, halt_flag | **None** — consensus is agnostic to which obfuscation variant ran |
| **Domain B (Admission/Execution)** | Blinded opcodes, cascade-derived variant config, attested execution | Polymorphic VM runs here; variant selected by cascade, not randomness |

### Why This Defeats Network-Level Blocking

1. **No Static Signatures Possible**
   - Variant selection is cascade-derived: `variant = cascade(validator_id || epoch || epoch_seed)`
   - Adversary cannot predict variant without epoch_seed (never transmitted)
   - Even with full network visibility, no reusable signature can be extracted

2. **No Behavioral Fingerprinting**
   - Execution is blinded: constant-time ops, ORAM access patterns, dummy chunk insertion
   - Power/timing/EM side-channels reveal nothing about which variant executed
   - Network traffic is uniform commitment packets (128 bytes), not execution traces

