   - QASH publishes no transaction graph — only cryptographic commitments
   - Traditional network analysis (flow graphs, timing correlation, mempool observation) has no substrate
   - Clone protocol (QR/NFC/BLE) decouples execution from network observation entirely

4. **Epoch-Bound Rotation**
   - Variant config changes every epoch automatically via cascade agility schedule
   - No governance or coordination required — deterministic, pre-authorized at genesis
   - Even if an adversary reverse-engineers one epoch's variant, it's useless for the next

### The Critical Distinction from Traditional Polymorphic Evasion

| Traditional Polymorphic Malware | QASH Polymorphic Execution |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------|
| Hides code *on* a public channel | Prevents channel from observing code at all |
| Relies on randomness (predictable with enough samples) | Uses cascade-derived determinism (unpredictable without epoch_seed) |
| Defender can still analyze network flow graphs | No public flow graph exists to analyze |
| Evasion is probabilistic ("hard to detect") | Evasion is architectural ("nothing to detect") |

