### `genesis()` factory

```rust
/// Create the initial protocol state (epoch 0, all-zero entropy, no halt).
/// §A0: Genesis state S_0 has halt_reason = None; all validator metrics = 0.
/// §1: validator_ids are stable, fixed at genesis.
///
/// `ids` is optional — if None, validator identities are auto-generated
/// sequentially (id[0][0] = 1, id[1][0] = 2, …). For production use,
/// always supply explicit ids derived from the genesis ceremony.
pub fn genesis(validator_count: u32, ids: Option<&[[u8; 48]]>) -> EpochState {
    assert!(
        validator_count as usize <= MAX_VALIDATORS,
        "validator_count exceeds MAX_VALIDATORS"
    );
    let mut state = EpochState {
        epoch: 0,
        halt_reason: HaltReason::None,
        entropy_seed: [0u8; 32],
        validators: [ValidatorMetrics::ZERO; MAX_VALIDATORS],
        validator_count,
        convergence_window: ConvergenceWindow::new(),
        nonces: [0u64; MAX_VALIDATORS],
        validator_ids: [[0u8; 48]; MAX_VALIDATORS],
        state_root: [0u8; 32],
    };
    match ids {
        Some(explicit) => {
            for (i, id) in explicit.iter().enumerate().take(validator_count as usize) {
                state.validator_ids[i] = *id;
            }
        }
        None => {
            for i in 0..validator_count as usize {
                state.validator_ids[i][0] = (i as u8) + 1; // synthetic, non-zero
            }
        }
    }
    state
}
```

### `step()` function

```rust
/// Execute one epoch transition and return the observation record.
/// This is T(S_t, I_t) from §E1 with explicit output capture.
/// On halt, StepOutput records the reason; subsequent calls to step()
/// on a halted state return the same halted StepOutput (§A6 absorbing).
///
/// Coq analogue: step in lyapunov_stability.v (TH-3a: no halt if δ ≤ ε)
pub fn step(state: &mut EpochState, input: &EpochInput) -> StepOutput {
    if state.is_halted() {
        // §A6 halt monotonicity: halted state is absorbing.
        return StepOutput {
            epoch: state.epoch,
            state_root: state.state_root,
            v_convergence: FixedPoint::ZERO,
            delta_window: FixedPoint::ZERO,
            halt_triggered: true,
            halt_reason: state.halt_reason,
        };
    }
    match advance_epoch(state, input, &[]) {
        Ok(result) => StepOutput {
            epoch: state.epoch,
            state_root: result.state_root,
            v_convergence: result.lyapunov.v_convergence,
            delta_window: result.lyapunov.delta_window,
            halt_triggered: false,
            halt_reason: HaltReason::None,
        },
        Err(reason) => StepOutput {
            epoch: state.epoch,
            state_root: state.state_root,
            v_convergence: FixedPoint::ZERO,
            delta_window: FixedPoint::ZERO,
            halt_triggered: true,
            halt_reason: reason,
        },
    }
}
```

### `run()` executor

```rust
/// Run a sequence of epoch inputs against a state, collecting one StepOutput
/// per epoch. Stops at first halt (absorbing) and returns all outputs up to
/// and including the halt epoch.
///
/// §A6: halt monotonicity guarantees run() always terminates.
/// §A1: run() is deterministic: same (state, inputs) → same outputs.
pub fn run(state: &mut EpochState, inputs: &[EpochInput]) -> Vec<StepOutput> {
    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(inputs.len());
    for input in inputs {
        let o = step(state, input);
        let halted = o.halt_triggered;
        out.push(o);
        if halted {
            break;
        }
    }
    out
}
```

