### Item 5b — `PublicTranscript` struct in `crates/consensus/src/public.rs` (new file)

The normative rule *"Raw transaction envelopes MUST NOT appear in `PublicTranscript`"*
currently relies on human review. Adding a typed struct makes this enforceable by the
Rust compiler: any Domain A code that inadvertently includes envelope fields in the
public surface will fail to compile.

```rust
//! Public observation transcript — the only Domain A artifacts
//! visible to external passive observers.
//!
//! RawTx, Tx envelopes, ValidatorMetrics, and ConvergenceWindow
//! are intentionally absent: they are Domain B admission artifacts.

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct PublicTranscript {
    pub state_root:   [u8; 32],
    pub receipt_root: [u8; 32],
    pub epoch:        u64,
    pub halt_flag:    bool,
}
```

Export from `lib.rs` as `pub use public::PublicTranscript;`.

This struct carries no logic — it is purely a type-system enforcement artifact
documenting the Domain A public surface boundary. `advance_epoch` in `transition.rs`
may optionally return a `PublicTranscript` (or the caller can construct one from the
returned `EpochState`).

