## 🔷 Core Sharding Design

### 1. Deterministic Shard Assignment (No Committees, No Coordination)
Validators are assigned to shards **cryptographically and epoch-bound**, eliminating coordination overhead and single points of failure:
```rust
// crates/consensus/src/shard_assignment.rs
pub fn assign_shards(
    epoch_seed: &[u8; 32],
    validator_id: u32,
    num_shards: u32,
) -> (u32, u32) {
    // Primary shard
    let primary = H_domain(ShardAssign, epoch_seed ∥ validator_id.to_be_bytes()) % num_shards;
    // Backup shard (for cross-shard sync redundancy)
    let backup = (primary + 1) % num_shards;
    (primary, backup)
}
```
